{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you back to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, thanks for coming. I just got discharged a couple days ago, but last night I ate a quarter of a sandwich and everything came back—severe pain, nausea, vomiting, fevers, chills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Where’s the pain located?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same as before—epigastric and right upper quadrant. It hasn’t changed in months. I couldn’t even walk to my clinic, so I went to the ER instead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really tough. Any pain meds since then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I got some relief at the other hospital, but nothing in the last few hours. It’s getting worse again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, we’ll get you some IV Dilaudid to help with that. You mentioned vomiting—have you kept anything down today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not even ice chips. I dry heaved earlier. I can usually keep pills down, but not today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ll start with IV meds and fluids for now. You’re on Zofran at home—want us to give that IV?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. And I haven’t had a bowel movement in two days. I can’t take my stool softeners by mouth. Can I get a suppository tomorrow morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-04-26 19:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We can give a Dulcolax suppository in the morning. Let’s focus on getting your nausea and pain under control first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pain med should be kicking in soon. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better, thank you. The sharpness is gone, but it’s still there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We reviewed your imaging from earlier today. The CT scan shows no signs of pancreatitis or kidney stones. Your gallbladder looks normal too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not pancreatitis again? But the pain feels just like the flares I’ve had before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The scan doesn’t show active inflammation. But we know your chronic pain is real. It’s possible this is a flare of your chronic pancreatitis, even if it’s not showing up on imaging."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve lost about 20 pounds since this all started. I’m worried I’m not getting enough nutrition. Should I be on TPN?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your albumin level—it’s normal at 3.8. That suggests your protein stores are okay for now. We don’t think TPN is needed, but we can connect you with a dietitian to talk about nutritional support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d really appreciate that. I’m trying to keep up with school, but missing classes is hard—even if I still have straight A’s."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great managing all this. We’ll make sure you’re stable before discharge. Now, about your methotrexate—your PCP is continuing it weekly?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, 25 mg weekly. I was supposed to see my doctor today to talk about increasing the dose, but I missed the appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We confirmed with their office. We’ll give you the methotrexate injection tonight. But the skin biopsy didn’t show vasculitis—so we’re not entirely sure what’s driving the inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is it still helping? I feel like I need something to keep this under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-04-26 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It may still be helping your malabsorption, which has improved. But we’re not seeing clear evidence of active vasculitis. Your PCP will help decide if the dose should go up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s your pain and nausea today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I haven’t vomited since last night. I might be able to try some liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll start you on clear liquids—water, broth, apple juice. If you keep that down, we’ll advance to full liquids, then regular food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my constipation? I had the suppository this morning and had a bowel movement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll switch to oral Senna and add bisacodyl as needed. Avoid narcotics when possible—they make it worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, but the pain is so bad sometimes I have to take the Dilaudid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. We’re balancing pain control with side effects. Your POTS is stable—we’re continuing fludrocortisone and betaxolol as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want another syncopal episode. I’m just frustrated—this keeps happening, and I don’t feel like anyone is coordinating my care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. We’ll make sure your PCP and specialists are updated. You’re seeing Dr. ___ soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not for a few weeks. I wish it were sooner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-04-27 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll flag that for your team. For now, focus on advancing your diet and staying hydrated. You’re making good progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-04-27 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well—tolerated full liquids, now moving to a regular diet. How’s the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-04-27 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I had a small meal and felt okay. Still some discomfort, but manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-04-27 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if this continues. No new medications—just your usual ones with a few adjustments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-04-27 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Adjustments? I thought I was going home on the same meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-04-27 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re lowering your escitalopram and betaxolol doses slightly—based on how you’re doing. You’ll take 10 mg escitalopram and 10 mg betaxolol daily. The rest stays the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-04-27 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s fine. And I’ll follow up with my doctors?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-04-27 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your PCP and specialists are aware. Try to keep those appointments—they’re important for managing your chronic conditions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-04-28 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made it through the night with no issues. We’ll discharge you in an hour or so. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-04-28 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just one—should I worry about the weight loss? I still feel like I’m not eating enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-04-28 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your albumin is normal, which is reassuring. Keep working with your care team on nutrition. Maybe ask your PCP for a dietitian referral."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-04-28 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you—for listening. It means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-04-28 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-04-26 19:04:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-04-28 11:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of chronic pancreatitis, vasculitis, POTS, and malabsorption was readmitted two days after discharge due to severe epigastric and right upper quadrant pain, nausea, and vomiting triggered by eating a small amount of food. She had persistent dry heaves and was unable to tolerate oral intake initially. Imaging showed no acute abdominal process, including no evidence of pancreatitis or obstruction. She was managed with IV pain control and anti-nausea medications, then gradually advanced to a regular diet. Methotrexate was administered after confirmation with her PCP, despite a skin biopsy not showing vasculitis. Constipation was addressed with a PR regimen and oral laxatives. Her anxiety and orthostatic hypotension were managed with continued home medications. She improved clinically, tolerated oral intake, and was discharged home with adjusted doses of escitalopram and betaxolol, and plans for outpatient follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Arteritis, unspecified",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Unspecified intestinal malabsorption",
      "Von Willebrand's disease",
      "Orthostatic hypotension",
      "Other constipation",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Other specified cardiac dysrhythmias"
    ]
  }
}
